# Shell scripts here are executed inside Linux containers, never on the host:
# the integration checks run in curlimages/curl, and init-dbs.sh is mounted into
# postgres. core.autocrlf is true on a Windows checkout, so without this rule a
# fresh clone rewrites them with CRLF and sh dies on the carriage return with an
# error that names the wrong thing entirely ("not found", pointing at a line
# that is plainly there). Keep them LF in the working tree on every platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
